Description: Annotates each sample of a post-mortem tissue cohort (GTEx or
    similar) with its position along two transcriptional axes of donor death
    derived from GTEx v8 across ten tissues, ventilator (perfused versus
    post-mortem) and prolonged agony, plus the ischemia component of the
    ventilator axis. For every sample it returns a signature score per axis,
    a position scaled between the two reference poles of the same tissue, the
    fraction of the sample's deviation from the tissue centroid that lies
    along the axes, a state label and technical contamination flags. Samples
    can then be plotted, selected with explicit criteria, and the per-sample
    scores used as covariates in differential-expression designs or
    batch-correction tools. compare_controls() repeats a case-versus-control
    differential expression with each candidate control subset against
    random subsets of the same size, optionally carrying a master-regulator
    analysis; annotate_de() and annotate_mra() annotate existing
    differential-expression and regulator tables with the axes their genes
    fall in; audit_report() writes the summary for a supplement.
